  "step_2": "The individual reports choosing Lottery B because the overall probability of winning any money is 25 percentage points higher in Lottery B than in Lottery A. The individual first calculates the amount of money to be won or lost, then weighs how much value they place on having any gain at all. The key justification is that they prefer having any gain (even if less than in A) over having no gain at all. This indicates a focus on the probability of winning something (i.e., avoiding zero), rather than on expected value or amount of money. The individual emphasizes the difference in winning probability (25% vs. 50%), which aligns with the decision reason's focus on the probability of a favorable outcome. The reasoning centers on the idea that having a chance to win something is more valuable than having no chance, which reflects a preference for higher probability of a favorable outcome, even if the amounts are not equal.",
